IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voc-common`
IMPORT `voc-core`
IMPORT `ctp-core`

-- Compensation for an injury caused by someone else outside work, in South Australia: victims of crime statutory
-- compensation (Victims of Crime Act 2001, Part 4) or a compulsory third party (CTP) claim after a motor accident (Motor
-- Vehicles Act 1959, Part 4; Civil Liability Act 1936, Part 8). SEAT OF THE INJURED PERSON.
--
-- SEAT: the person injured -- the victim of an offence, or a family member claiming for grief, the dependants' loss or
-- funeral expenses; or a person injured in a motor accident. "Which scheme covers me? Am I eligible? By when must I apply
-- or give notice, and to whom? What must I send? What can I get, and what limits apply?" Every question is phrased as
-- that person asks it, on facts that person could state; where a fact is the court's or another person's judgment, the
-- @desc says so. The rules are in voc-core.l4 and ctp-core.l4; this module builds their records from plain answers and
-- restates no rule.
--
-- THE JOIN: Victims of Crime Act s 17(5)(c). A victim whose injury falls within the CTP scheme (for example, one hit by a
-- dangerous driver) gets no statutory compensation and claims under the CTP part instead; s 17(5)(b) sends an injury
-- covered by a Return to Work payment for death or non-economic loss to that Act. The first question decides the route.
--
-- TEXTS: the Open Australian Legal Corpus texts (not official, possibly out of date); see voc-core.l4, ctp-core.l4 and
-- NOTES.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Injured by someone else -- the injured person's questions`

§§ `Which scheme covers me`

DECLARE `Which scheme` IS ONE OF
    `the CTP scheme: give notice of your claim to the vehicle's CTP insurer (Motor Vehicles Act s 126A); no victims of crime statutory compensation (s 17(5)(c))`
    `the CTP scheme: give notice of your claim to the nominal defendant (Motor Vehicles Act ss 115, 116, 126A); no victims of crime statutory compensation (s 17(5)(c))`
    `another State's or Territory's CTP scheme, not covered here; no victims of crime statutory compensation (s 17(5)(c))`
    `the Return to Work Act 2014; no victims of crime statutory compensation (s 17(5)(b))`
    `victims of crime statutory compensation, if you are eligible (Victims of Crime Act s 17)`
    `neither scheme in this encoding: no offence, and no CTP claim`
    `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013 or an offence before 1 July 2015`

@export Which scheme covers my injury: victims of crime statutory compensation, or a compulsory third party (CTP) motor accident claim (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 17(5)(b), (c); Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) ss 99(3), 115, 116)?
GIVEN `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day of the offence or accident that injured you (or caused the death you are claiming for)
      `it was a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what happened was a criminal offence, such as an assault, a sexual offence or dangerous driving (it counts even if the offender was too young or mentally impaired to be guilty)
      `a motor vehicle was involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a motor vehicle (a car, motorbike, truck or bus, but not a train or tram) was involved in causing the injury
      `how the vehicle caused it` IS A `How the motor vehicle caused the injury` @desc How the vehicle caused the injury: as a direct consequence of its being driven, of its running out of control, of a person travelling on a road colliding with it while it was stationary (or avoiding that), or in some other way (for example, an assault inside a parked car); if no vehicle was involved, any answer
      `it was a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was caused by a terrorist act
      `the vehicle's insurance` IS A `The vehicle's insurance` @desc The vehicle's insurance: insured under South Australian CTP (every registered vehicle is), insured under another State's or Territory's CTP law, covered by other insurance the Motor Vehicles Act accepts (some farm machines and exempt vehicles), uninsured, or never identified after due inquiry and search (a hit-and-run); if no vehicle was involved, any answer
      `the vehicle was on a road` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was on a road when it caused the injury (matters only for an uninsured vehicle)
      `I have a Return to Work payment for the same harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have received, or are entitled to, a payment or damages for death or non-economic loss for the same harm under the Return to Work Act 2014 (workers compensation)
GIVETH A `Which scheme`
DECIDE `Which scheme covers my injury` IS
    IF `a motor vehicle was involved` AND `who answers` EQUALS `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`
    THEN `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013 or an offence before 1 July 2015`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the s 17(5)(b), (c) exclusion` `the s 17(5) facts`
         WHEN JUST e THEN
             IF e EQUALS `not entitled: a Return to Work payment or damages covers the same harm (s 17(5)(b))`
             THEN `the Return to Work Act 2014; no victims of crime statutory compensation (s 17(5)(b))`
             ELSE IF `who answers` EQUALS `the vehicle's CTP insurer (s 126A(1))`
                  THEN `the CTP scheme: give notice of your claim to the vehicle's CTP insurer (Motor Vehicles Act s 126A); no victims of crime statutory compensation (s 17(5)(c))`
                  ELSE IF `the claim is against the nominal defendant` `who answers`
                       THEN `the CTP scheme: give notice of your claim to the nominal defendant (Motor Vehicles Act ss 115, 116, 126A); no victims of crime statutory compensation (s 17(5)(c))`
                       ELSE `another State's or Territory's CTP scheme, not covered here; no victims of crime statutory compensation (s 17(5)(c))`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             IF NOT `it was a criminal offence`
             THEN `neither scheme in this encoding: no offence, and no CTP claim`
             ELSE IF `the offence is within this encoding` `the day it happened`
                  THEN `victims of crime statutory compensation, if you are eligible (Victims of Crime Act s 17)`
                  ELSE `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013 or an offence before 1 July 2015`
    WHERE
        `the accident` MEANS
            `The motor accident` WITH
                `the day of the accident`             IS `the day it happened`
                `how the vehicle caused the injury`   IS `how the vehicle caused it`
                `it was a terrorist act`              IS `it was a terrorist act`
                `the vehicle's insurance`             IS `the vehicle's insurance`
                `the vehicle was on a road`           IS `the vehicle was on a road`
        `who answers` MEANS `who answers the CTP claim` `the accident`
        `the s 17(5) facts` MEANS
            `Section 17(5) facts` WITH
                -- (a) and (e) do not decide the route; placeholders, read by no rule used here.
                `the injury arises from a breach of statutory duty by the person's employer in the course of the person's employment` IS FALSE
                `the person has received or is entitled to a Return to Work payment or damages for death or non-economic loss for the same harm` IS `I have a Return to Work payment for the same harm`
                `the injury falls within the ambit of a compulsory third-party insurance scheme covering a motor vehicle` IS (`a motor vehicle was involved` AND `the injury falls within the ambit of a CTP scheme` `the accident`)
                `the person is a prisoner claiming for psychological injury from an offence committed in the prison` IS FALSE
                `the prisoner was assaulted or suffered physical injury` IS FALSE

§§ `Victims of crime -- am I eligible` -- situation: you were hurt by a crime, or a member of your family died of one

@export Am I eligible to claim victims of crime statutory compensation for my own injury (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 4(1), s 17(1), (5))?
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed
      `it involved violence or a threat of violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence involved violence, or a threat of violence, against you or a member of your immediate family (spouse or domestic partner, parent, grandparent, child, grandchild, brother or sister)
      `it made me reasonably fear imminent harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence created a reasonable apprehension of imminent harm to you or a member of your immediate family
      `it was a sexual offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence was a sexual offence
      `it caused death or physical injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence caused anyone's death or physical injury
      `I was physically injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered physical injury as a result of the offence
      `I was psychologically injured by being directly involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered psychological injury from being directly involved in the offence, or in dealing with its immediate aftermath
      `I suffered other harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered any other injury, damage or loss as a result of the offence (mental injury includes shock and nervous shock)
      `it was committed against my child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence was committed against a child under 18 of whom you are a parent or guardian
      `my relationship to someone who died of it` IS A `Family relationship` @desc If someone died as a result of the offence, how you are related to them; otherwise `none of these`
      `I took part in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a party to committing the offence
      `my employer's breach of statutory duty caused it at work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury arose from your employer's breach of a statutory duty in the course of your employment
      `I have a Return to Work payment for the same harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have received, or are entitled to, a Return to Work Act 2014 payment or damages for death or non-economic loss for the same harm
      `my injury falls within the CTP scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury falls within a compulsory third party (CTP) scheme (see the question "Which scheme covers my injury")
      `I am a prisoner claiming for psychological injury from an offence in prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a prisoner claiming for psychological injury from an offence committed in the prison
      `I was assaulted or physically injured in prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are such a prisoner, whether you were assaulted or physically injured
GIVETH AN `Eligibility`
DECIDE `Am I eligible to claim for my injury` IS
    `s 17(1) -- eligibility to claim for injury` `the offence` `me` `the exclusions`
    WHERE
        `the offence` MEANS
            `The offence` WITH
                `the day the offence was committed` IS `the day of the offence`
                `it involved violence or a threat of violence against the person or a member of the person's immediate family` IS `it involved violence or a threat of violence`
                `it created a reasonable apprehension of imminent harm to the person or a member of the person's immediate family` IS `it made me reasonably fear imminent harm`
                `it is a sexual offence` IS `it was a sexual offence`
                `it caused death or physical injury` IS `it caused death or physical injury`
                `it is a homicide` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: s 17(1) does not read it
        `me` MEANS
            `The person and the offence` WITH
                `the person suffered physical injury as a result of the offence` IS `I was physically injured`
                `the person suffered psychological injury from being directly involved in the offence or its immediate aftermath` IS `I was psychologically injured by being directly involved`
                `the person suffered other harm (injury, damage or loss) as a result of the offence` IS `I suffered other harm`
                `the offence was committed against a child of whom the person is a parent or guardian` IS `it was committed against my child`
                `the person's relationship to someone who died as a result of the offence` IS `my relationship to someone who died of it`
                `the person was a party to the commission of the offence` IS `I took part in the offence`
        `the exclusions` MEANS
            `Section 17(5) facts` WITH
                `the injury arises from a breach of statutory duty by the person's employer in the course of the person's employment` IS `my employer's breach of statutory duty caused it at work`
                `the person has received or is entitled to a Return to Work payment or damages for death or non-economic loss for the same harm` IS `I have a Return to Work payment for the same harm`
                `the injury falls within the ambit of a compulsory third-party insurance scheme covering a motor vehicle` IS `my injury falls within the CTP scheme`
                `the person is a prisoner claiming for psychological injury from an offence committed in the prison` IS `I am a prisoner claiming for psychological injury from an offence in prison`
                `the prisoner was assaulted or suffered physical injury` IS `I was assaulted or physically injured in prison`

-- The Section 17(5) facts for a claim arising from a death: (a) and (e) are not applied (voc-core.l4, reading).
GIVEN `I have a Return to Work payment for the same harm` IS A BOOLEAN, `the death falls within the CTP scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Section 17(5) facts`
`the s 17(5) facts for a death claim` `I have a Return to Work payment for the same harm` `the death falls within the CTP scheme` MEANS
    `Section 17(5) facts` WITH
        `the injury arises from a breach of statutory duty by the person's employer in the course of the person's employment` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: not applied to a death claim
        `the person has received or is entitled to a Return to Work payment or damages for death or non-economic loss for the same harm` IS `I have a Return to Work payment for the same harm`
        `the injury falls within the ambit of a compulsory third-party insurance scheme covering a motor vehicle` IS `the death falls within the CTP scheme`
        `the person is a prisoner claiming for psychological injury from an offence committed in the prison` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: not applied to a death claim
        `the prisoner was assaulted or suffered physical injury` IS FALSE  -- placeholder

GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE, `it was a homicide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The offence`
`the offence that caused the death` `the day of the offence` `it was a homicide` MEANS
    `The offence` WITH
        `the day the offence was committed` IS `the day of the offence`
        -- placeholders: ss 17(2)-(4) do not read the s 17(1)(b) conditions
        `it involved violence or a threat of violence against the person or a member of the person's immediate family` IS FALSE
        `it created a reasonable apprehension of imminent harm to the person or a member of the person's immediate family` IS FALSE
        `it is a sexual offence` IS FALSE
        `it caused death or physical injury` IS TRUE
        `it is a homicide` IS `it was a homicide`

@export Am I eligible to claim victims of crime statutory compensation for grief after a homicide (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 17(2), (5))?
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence that caused the death was committed
      `it was a homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death was caused by murder, manslaughter, or criminal neglect where the victim died
      `my relationship to the deceased` IS A `Relationship to the deceased` @desc How you were related to the person who died: spouse or domestic partner, child (under 18, or 18 or over, at the time of the offence), parent, or other
      `the deceased was under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was under 18
      `I have a Return to Work payment for the same harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have received, or are entitled to, a Return to Work Act 2014 payment or damages for the death
      `the death falls within the CTP scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death falls within a compulsory third party (CTP) scheme, for example because it was caused by driving (see the question "Which scheme covers my injury")
GIVETH AN `Eligibility`
DECIDE `Am I eligible to claim for grief` IS
    `s 17(2) -- eligibility to claim for grief` (`the offence that caused the death` `the day of the offence` `it was a homicide`) `my relationship to the deceased` `the deceased was under 18` (`the s 17(5) facts for a death claim` `I have a Return to Work payment for the same harm` `the death falls within the CTP scheme`)

@export Am I eligible to claim victims of crime statutory compensation for the financial loss of the dependants of a person who died (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 17(3), (5))?
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed
      `the victim died of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim died as a result of the injury the offence caused
      `an order has already been made for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has already made an order for statutory compensation for that injury
      `the court finds me suitable to represent the dependants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers you a suitable person to represent the interests of the dependants (the spouse, domestic partner, parents or children who were financially dependent on the victim); this is the court's opinion
      `a dependant has a Return to Work payment for the same harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Return to Work Act 2014 payment or damages for the death has been received or is due for the same harm
      `the death falls within the CTP scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death falls within a compulsory third party (CTP) scheme (see the question "Which scheme covers my injury")
GIVETH AN `Eligibility`
DECIDE `Am I eligible to claim for the dependants' loss` IS
    `s 17(3) -- eligibility to claim for the dependants' financial loss` (`the offence that caused the death` `the day of the offence` FALSE) `the victim died of the injury` `an order has already been made for the injury` `the court finds me suitable to represent the dependants` (`the s 17(5) facts for a death claim` `a dependant has a Return to Work payment for the same harm` `the death falls within the CTP scheme`)

@export Am I eligible to claim victims of crime statutory compensation for a victim's funeral expenses (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 17(4), (5))?
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed
      `the victim died because of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim died in consequence of the offence
      `I paid or must pay for the funeral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid, or are responsible for paying, the victim's funeral expenses
      `I have a Return to Work payment for the same harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have received, or are entitled to, a Return to Work Act 2014 payment or damages for the death
      `the death falls within the CTP scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death falls within a compulsory third party (CTP) scheme (see the question "Which scheme covers my injury")
GIVETH AN `Eligibility`
DECIDE `Am I eligible to claim funeral expenses` IS
    `s 17(4) -- eligibility to claim funeral expenses` (`the offence that caused the death` `the day of the offence` FALSE) `the victim died because of the offence` `I paid or must pay for the funeral` (`the s 17(5) facts for a death claim` `I have a Return to Work payment for the same harm` `the death falls within the CTP scheme`)

§§ `Victims of crime -- applying` -- situation: you are eligible and want to claim

@export By what date must I apply to the Crown Solicitor for victims of crime statutory compensation (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 18(1)-(3), (7))?
GIVEN `what I am applying for` IS A `Kind of application` @desc Whether you are applying for your own injury as a victim, or for grief, the dependants' loss or funeral expenses after a victim's death
      `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day the victim died (any day if no one died)
      `the court has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the District Court has extended the time to apply
      `the day the court extended it to` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it was extended to (otherwise any day)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I apply to the Crown Solicitor` IS
    `the last day, as extended under s 18(7)` (`the last day of the initial application period` `what I am applying for` `the day of the offence` `the day of death`) `the court has extended the time` `the day the court extended it to`

DECLARE `Court application window` HAS
    `the first day I may apply to the court`  IS A DATE
    `the last day I may apply to the court`   IS A DATE

-- READING: s 18(5) lets the claimant apply once the claim "has not been settled ... within" the period for negotiation,
-- so the first day is the day after that period ends.
@export If the Crown Solicitor and I do not settle my victims of crime claim, from when may I apply to the District Court, and by what date (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 18(5)-(7))?
GIVEN `what I am applying for` IS A `Kind of application` @desc Whether you applied for your own injury as a victim, or for grief, the dependants' loss or funeral expenses after a victim's death
      `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day the victim died (any day if no one died)
      `the day I applied to the Crown Solicitor` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your application to the Crown Solicitor
      `we agreed a longer period for negotiation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the Crown Solicitor agreed a period for negotiation longer than 3 months
      `the day the agreed period ends` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day of the agreed period (otherwise any day)
      `the court has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the District Court has extended the time to apply to it
      `the day the court extended it to` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it was extended to (otherwise any day)
GIVETH A `Court application window`
DECIDE `When may I apply to the court` IS
    `Court application window` WITH
        `the first day I may apply to the court` IS `the end of negotiation` `plus days` 1
        `the last day I may apply to the court`  IS `the last day, as extended under s 18(7)` (`the last day to apply to the court (s 18(6))` (`the last day of the initial application period` `what I am applying for` `the day of the offence` `the day of death`) `the end of negotiation`) `the court has extended the time` `the day the court extended it to`
    WHERE
        `the end of negotiation` MEANS `the last day of the period for negotiation` `the day I applied to the Crown Solicitor` `we agreed a longer period for negotiation` `the day the agreed period ends`

@export If I apply to the District Court for victims of crime statutory compensation, must I serve a copy of my application on the offender (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 19(2), (3))?
GIVEN `I know who the offender is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the identity of the offender is known
      `the court has exempted me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court, on your application, has exempted you from serving the offender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I serve the offender` IF
    `the claimant must serve the offender (s 19(2), (3))` `I know who the offender is` `the court has exempted me`

@export What must my application to the Crown Solicitor for victims of crime statutory compensation contain or have with it (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 18(4); Victims of Crime (Statutory Compensation) Regulations 2019 (SA) reg 4, Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `I am not the victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are claiming as someone other than the victim (for example, a family member)
      `I rely on my relationship to the victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim relies on your relationship to the victim
      `the victim has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim is dead
      `I claim only grief or funeral expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is only for grief, funeral expenses or both (a "limited claim")
      `I claim only funeral expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is only for funeral expenses
      `I claim special damages or lost earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim special damages (such as treatment costs) or loss of earnings
      `I claim past lost earnings as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim earnings you lost as an employee
      `I claim past lost earnings as self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim earnings you lost as a self-employed person
      `I claim lost work under a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim earnings lost because the injury stopped you entering into or carrying out a contract with someone
      `I claim loss of earning capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim loss of earning capacity (ongoing lost earnings)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Application item`
DECIDE `What must my application contain` IS
    `what the application must contain (s 18(4), reg 4, Schedule 1)`
        (`What the application claims` WITH
            `the claimant is not the victim`                                   IS `I am not the victim`
            `the claimant relies on a relationship to the victim`              IS `I rely on my relationship to the victim`
            `the victim is dead`                                               IS `the victim has died`
            `the claim is limited to grief, funeral expenses or both`          IS `I claim only grief or funeral expenses`
            `the claim is limited to funeral expenses`                         IS `I claim only funeral expenses`
            `special damages or loss of earnings are claimed`                  IS `I claim special damages or lost earnings`
            `past loss of earnings is claimed as an employee`                  IS `I claim past lost earnings as an employee`
            `past loss of earnings is claimed as a self-employed person`       IS `I claim past lost earnings as self-employed`
            `loss of earnings from a contract the injury prevented is claimed` IS `I claim lost work under a contract`
            `loss of earning capacity is claimed`                              IS `I claim loss of earning capacity`)

§§ `Victims of crime -- how much` -- situation: you are eligible and want to know the amounts

GIVEN `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` IS A NUMBER, `CPI for the September quarter 2014` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `CPI figures for s 4(2)`
`the CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` `CPI for the September quarter 2014` MEANS
    `CPI figures for s 4(2)` WITH
        `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the adjustment` IS `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence`
        `CPI for the September quarter 2014`                               IS `CPI for the September quarter 2014`

GIVEN `my claim breaks the s 20(5) rule` IS A BOOLEAN, `it would be unjust not to compensate me` IS A BOOLEAN, `I failed to report or co-operate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Court findings under s 20`
`the court's findings` `my claim breaks the s 20(5) rule` `it would be unjust not to compensate me` `I failed to report or co-operate` MEANS
    `Court findings under s 20` WITH
        `the court finds the claimant's indictable conduct contributed materially to the injury or death (s 20(5), (5a))` IS `my claim breaks the s 20(5) rule`
        `the court finds that failure to compensate would be unjust`                                                     IS `it would be unjust not to compensate me`
        `the court finds a failure without good reason to report or co-operate that hindered the case (s 20(7))`        IS `I failed to report or co-operate`

@export What are the indexed limits on victims of crime statutory compensation for my offence: the overall limit, the most for grief and the most for funeral expenses (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 4(2), s 20, s 34)?
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed (amounts are those in force then, s 34)
      `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the year of the offence, as published by the ABS (ignored for an offence before 2016)
      `CPI for the September quarter 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter 2014, as published by the ABS (ignored for an offence before 2016)
GIVETH AN `Indexed amounts`
DECIDE `What are the indexed limits for my offence` IS
    `the indexed amounts for an offence on` `the day of the offence` `with` (`the CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` `CPI for the September quarter 2014`)

@export How much victims of crime statutory compensation can I be awarded for my own injury, given the court's assessment (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 20(1)(a), (3)(a), (5), (7), (9), Schedule a1)?
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed
      `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the year of the offence (ignored for an offence before 2016)
      `CPI for the September quarter 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter 2014 (ignored for an offence before 2016)
      `my financial loss` IS A NUMBER @desc Your financial loss in dollars as the court would otherwise assess it (lost earnings, expenses), leaving out hospital or medical expenses a health fund or scheme would pay, and after any reduction for your own conduct or failure to mitigate (s 20(4), (8)); 0 if none
      `the scale value for my non-financial loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The number from 0 to 60 the court assigns to your pain and suffering, loss of amenities and of expectation of life, and disfigurement (s 20(3)(a)(ii))
      `my claim breaks the s 20(5) rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds you were injured while committing an indictable offence that contributed materially to the risk of injury
      `it would be unjust not to compensate me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the court is satisfied that failing to compensate you would be unjust
      `I failed to report or co-operate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds that you, without good reason, failed to report the offence in reasonable time or to co-operate with police or the prosecution, and that this stopped or significantly hindered the case (s 20(7))
GIVETH AN `Award`
DECIDE `How much can I be awarded for my injury` IS
    `s 20(1)(a), (3)(a) -- the award for injury` `the day of the offence` (`the CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` `CPI for the September quarter 2014`) `my financial loss` `the scale value for my non-financial loss` (`the court's findings` `my claim breaks the s 20(5) rule` `it would be unjust not to compensate me` `I failed to report or co-operate`)

@export How much victims of crime statutory compensation can I be awarded for grief after a homicide (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 20(1)(c), (5a), (7))?
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed
      `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the year of the offence (ignored for an offence before 2016)
      `CPI for the September quarter 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter 2014 (ignored for an offence before 2016)
      `the amount the court thinks fit` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in dollars the court thinks fit for your grief, before the limit
      `my conduct contributed to the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the death happened while you were committing an indictable offence that contributed materially to it (s 20(5a))
      `it would be unjust not to compensate me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the court is satisfied that failing to compensate you would be unjust
      `I failed to report or co-operate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds that you, without good reason, failed to report the offence or to co-operate with police or the prosecution, and that this stopped or significantly hindered the case (s 20(7))
GIVETH AN `Award`
DECIDE `How much can I be awarded for grief` IS
    `s 20(1)(c) -- the award for grief` `the day of the offence` (`the CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` `CPI for the September quarter 2014`) `the amount the court thinks fit` (`the court's findings` `my conduct contributed to the death` `it would be unjust not to compensate me` `I failed to report or co-operate`)

@export How much victims of crime statutory compensation can I be awarded for a victim's funeral expenses (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 20(1)(d), (5a), (7))?
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed
      `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the year of the offence (ignored for an offence before 2016)
      `CPI for the September quarter 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter 2014 (ignored for an offence before 2016)
      `the funeral expenses I incurred` IS A NUMBER @desc The funeral expenses you incurred, in dollars
      `my conduct contributed to the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the death happened while you were committing an indictable offence that contributed materially to it (s 20(5a))
      `it would be unjust not to compensate me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the court is satisfied that failing to compensate you would be unjust
      `I failed to report or co-operate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds that you, without good reason, failed to report the offence or to co-operate with police or the prosecution, and that this stopped or significantly hindered the case (s 20(7))
GIVETH AN `Award`
DECIDE `How much can I be awarded for funeral expenses` IS
    `s 20(1)(d) -- the award for funeral expenses` `the day of the offence` (`the CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` `CPI for the September quarter 2014`) `the funeral expenses I incurred` (`the court's findings` `my conduct contributed to the death` `it would be unjust not to compensate me` `I failed to report or co-operate`)

@export How much victims of crime statutory compensation can be awarded for the dependants' financial loss after a victim's death (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 20(1)(b), (3)(a), (7))?
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed
      `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the year of the offence (ignored for an offence before 2016)
      `CPI for the September quarter 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter 2014 (ignored for an offence before 2016)
      `the dependants' financial loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The dependants' financial loss in dollars as the court would otherwise assess it
      `I failed to report or co-operate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds that you, without good reason, failed to report the offence or to co-operate with police or the prosecution, and that this stopped or significantly hindered the case (s 20(7))
GIVETH AN `Award`
DECIDE `How much can be awarded for the dependants' loss` IS
    `s 20(1)(b), (3)(a) -- the award for the dependants' financial loss` `the day of the offence` (`the CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` `CPI for the September quarter 2014`) `the dependants' financial loss` (`the court's findings` FALSE FALSE `I failed to report or co-operate`)

@export If I claim victims of crime statutory compensation in more than one capacity, what is the most I can be awarded in all (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 20(3)(c))?
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed
      `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the year of the offence (ignored for an offence before 2016)
      `CPI for the September quarter 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter 2014 (ignored for an offence before 2016)
      `my award for injury` IS A NUMBER @desc The award for your own injury, in dollars (see "How much ... for my own injury"; 0 if none)
      `my award for grief` IS A NUMBER @desc The award for grief, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the award for the dependants' loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The award you claim as the dependants' representative, in dollars (0 if none)
      `my award for funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc The award for funeral expenses, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be awarded in all` IS
    `s 20(3)(c) -- the most one claimant can be awarded in all` `my award for injury` `my award for grief` `the award for the dependants' loss` `my award for funeral expenses` (amounts's `the overall limit (s 20(3)(a)(iii), (c))`)
    WHERE
        amounts MEANS `the indexed amounts for an offence on` `the day of the offence` `with` (`the CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the offence` `CPI for the September quarter 2014`)

@export What is the most my lawyer may charge me, or the court award, for legal costs on my victims of crime claim, before GST (Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA) s 25(1); Victims of Crime (Statutory Compensation) Regulations 2019 (SA) reg 5, Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `the day the proceedings commenced` IS A DATE @desc The day the proceedings on your claim commenced (the amounts in force then apply)
      `CPI for the September quarter of the year before` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the year the proceedings commenced (ignored before 2016)
      `CPI for the September quarter 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter 2014 (ignored before 2016)
      `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim for legal costs` @desc Whether yours is a limited claim (grief or funeral expenses only), the first or another of related claims (one lawyer acting for several victims of the same offence or series), or any other claim
      `the offender is known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the identity of the offender is known
      `compensation was agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether compensation was agreed (settled) with the Crown
      `I applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an application to the court for compensation was made (counsel's fees)
      `hours of the hearing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours the court hearing took (0 if none)
      `the court must approve a settlement for a person under a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is by a person under a legal disability (such as a child) whose settlement needs the court's approval
      `there was an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there was an appeal
GIVETH A `Legal costs answer`
DECIDE `What is the most my lawyer may charge` IS
    `s 25(1) -- the most that may be charged or awarded for costs` `the day the proceedings commenced` (`the CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before` `CPI for the September quarter 2014`)
        (`Legal costs facts` WITH
            `kind of claim`                                    IS `the kind of claim`
            `the identity of the offender is known`            IS `the offender is known`
            `compensation is agreed`                           IS `compensation was agreed`
            `an application to the court for compensation is made` IS `I applied to the court`
            `hours of the hearing of the application`          IS `hours of the hearing`
            `the claim is by a person under a disability and the court must approve the settlement` IS `the court must approve a settlement for a person under a disability`
            `there is an appeal`                               IS `there was an appeal`)

§§ `Motor accident (CTP) -- whom to notify, by when, with what` -- situation: you were injured in a motor accident

GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE, how IS A `How the motor vehicle caused the injury`, `terrorist` IS A BOOLEAN, `insurance` IS A `The vehicle's insurance`, `on a road` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The motor accident`
`my motor accident` `the day of the accident` how `terrorist` `insurance` `on a road` MEANS
    `The motor accident` WITH
        `the day of the accident`             IS `the day of the accident`
        `how the vehicle caused the injury`   IS how
        `it was a terrorist act`              IS `terrorist`
        `the vehicle's insurance`             IS `insurance`
        `the vehicle was on a road`           IS `on a road`

@export Whom must I give my compulsory third party (CTP) notice of claim to: the vehicle's insurer or the nominal defendant (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) ss 99(3), 115, 116, 126A(1))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `how the vehicle caused my injury` IS A `How the motor vehicle caused the injury` @desc How the vehicle caused your injury: as a direct consequence of its being driven, of its running out of control, of a person travelling on a road colliding with it while it was stationary (or avoiding that), or in some other way
      `it was a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was caused by a terrorist act
      `the vehicle's insurance` IS A `The vehicle's insurance` @desc The vehicle's insurance: insured under South Australian CTP, under another State's or Territory's CTP law, covered by other insurance the Act accepts, uninsured, or never identified after due inquiry and search
      `the vehicle was on a road` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was on a road (matters only for an uninsured vehicle)
GIVETH A `Who answers the claim`
DECIDE `Whom must I give my notice of claim to` IS
    `who answers the CTP claim` (`my motor accident` `the day of the accident` `how the vehicle caused my injury` `it was a terrorist act` `the vehicle's insurance` `the vehicle was on a road`)

@export By when must I give notice of my compulsory third party (CTP) claim (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) s 126A(2)(a), ss 115(3), 116(4); Motor Vehicles (Third Party Insurance) Regulations 2013 (SA) reg 4(1))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `how the vehicle caused my injury` IS A `How the motor vehicle caused the injury` @desc How the vehicle caused your injury: as a direct consequence of its being driven, of its running out of control, of a collision on a road with it while stationary (or avoiding that), or in some other way
      `it was a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was caused by a terrorist act
      `the vehicle's insurance` IS A `The vehicle's insurance` @desc The vehicle's insurance: insured under South Australian CTP, under another State's or Territory's CTP law, covered by other insurance the Act accepts, uninsured, or never identified after due inquiry and search
      `the vehicle was on a road` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was on a road (matters only for an uninsured vehicle)
      `the day it became apparent` IS A DATE @desc For an unidentified or uninsured vehicle, the day it became apparent that the vehicle could not readily be identified, or was uninsured (otherwise any day)
GIVETH A `Notice deadline`
DECIDE `By when must I give notice of my claim` IS
    `the time for the notice of claim (s 126A(2)(a), reg 4(1))` (`who answers the CTP claim` (`my motor accident` `the day of the accident` `how the vehicle caused my injury` `it was a terrorist act` `the vehicle's insurance` `the vehicle was on a road`)) `the day of the accident` `the day it became apparent`

@export What must my compulsory third party (CTP) notice of claim include or have with it (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) s 126A(2); Motor Vehicles (Third Party Insurance) Regulations 2013 (SA) regs 5, 6)?
GIVEN `the accident was reported to police` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident was reported to a police officer under the Road Traffic Act 1961
      `I claim lost income or earning capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim includes loss of income or earning capacity
      `I claim medical expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim includes payment of medical expenses
      `I claim for a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim relates to a death and is brought under Part 5 of the Civil Liability Act 1936
      `I was driving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured while driving a motor vehicle
GIVETH A LIST OF `Notice item`
DECIDE `What must my notice of claim include` IS
    `what the notice of claim must include (s 126A(2), reg 5, reg 6)`
        (`What the CTP claim includes` WITH
            `the accident was reported to a police officer under the Road Traffic Act 1961` IS `the accident was reported to police`
            `the claim includes loss of income or earning capacity`                        IS `I claim lost income or earning capacity`
            `the claim includes payment of medical expenses`                               IS `I claim medical expenses`
            `the claim relates to a death and is brought under Part 5 of the Civil Liability Act 1936` IS `I claim for a death`
            `the claimant was injured while driving a motor vehicle`                       IS `I was driving`)

GIVEN `in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN, `with everything required` IS A BOOLEAN, `with the access authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `why late` IS A `Why the notice was late`, `prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Compliance with s 126A`
`my notice` `in the approved form` `with everything required` `with the access authority` `why late` `prejudiced` MEANS
    `Compliance with s 126A` WITH
        `the notice was in the manner and form the Minister approves (s 126A(2)(b))`             IS `in the approved form`
        `the notice set out or was accompanied by everything s 126A(2)(c) and reg 5 require`      IS `with everything required`
        `the notice was accompanied by the access authority (s 126A(2)(d))`                      IS `with the access authority`
        `why the notice was late`                                                                 IS `why late`
        `the proper assessment of the claim has been substantially prejudiced by the lateness`   IS `prejudiced`

@export May the CTP insurer or the nominal defendant refuse to consider or deal with my claim because of my notice (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) s 126A(6)(a), (7); Motor Vehicles (Third Party Insurance) Regulations 2013 (SA) reg 4(2))?
GIVEN `my notice was in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your notice of claim was in the manner and form the Minister approves
      `my notice had everything required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it set out or came with the claim details, the medical certificate, the police report number and the documents reg 5 requires (see "What must my notice of claim include")
      `my notice had the access authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it came with the signed statement authorising access to your records
      `why my notice was late` IS A `Why the notice was late` @desc If your notice was late: ignorance or mistake, absence from the State, your injury, your legal disability, another reasonable cause, or none of these; otherwise `it was not late`
      `the lateness substantially prejudiced the assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was late, whether the proper assessment of your claim has been substantially prejudiced (a judgment for the insurer or the court)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the insurer refuse to deal with my claim` IF
    `the insurer or nominal defendant may decline to consider or deal with the claim (s 126A(6)(a))` (`my notice` `my notice was in the approved form` `my notice had everything required` `my notice had the access authority` `why my notice was late` `the lateness substantially prejudiced the assessment`)

@export Can I start, or continue, court proceedings on my compulsory third party (CTP) claim (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) s 126A(6)(b); Motor Vehicles (Third Party Insurance) Regulations 2013 (SA) reg 4(3))?
GIVEN `my notice was in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your notice of claim was in the manner and form the Minister approves
      `my notice had everything required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have provided the claim details, the medical certificate, the police report number and the documents reg 5 requires
      `my notice had the access authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have provided the signed statement authorising access to your records
      `why my notice was late` IS A `Why the notice was late` @desc If your notice was late, why; otherwise `it was not late`
      `the lateness substantially prejudiced the assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was late, whether the proper assessment of your claim has been substantially prejudiced
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I start or continue proceedings` IF
    `the claimant may commence or continue proceedings (s 126A(6)(b), reg 4(3))` (`my notice` `my notice was in the approved form` `my notice had everything required` `my notice had the access authority` `why my notice was late` `the lateness substantially prejudiced the assessment`)

@export By what date must the CTP insurer or the nominal defendant send me a copy of a record it obtained with my access authority (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) s 126A(4))?
GIVEN `the day it received the record` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer or nominal defendant received the record or information under your access authority
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the insurer send me a copy` IS
    `the day it received the record` `plus days` `the days to send the claimant a copy (s 126A(4))`

@export Can my action against the nominal defendant be dismissed because I did not give notice as soon as reasonably practicable (Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA) ss 115(4), 116(5))?
GIVEN `I gave notice as soon as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the nominal defendant written notice of the claim, with a short statement of its grounds, as soon as reasonably practicable after it became apparent that the vehicle could not be identified or was uninsured
      `the court finds the defence was prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that the nominal defendant's defence was prejudiced by a late notice (the court's finding)
      `the justice of the case requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers the justice of the case requires dismissal (the court's judgment)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my action be dismissed for late notice` IF
    `the court may dismiss the action against the nominal defendant (s 115(4), s 116(5))` `I gave notice as soon as reasonably practicable` `the court finds the defence was prejudiced` `the justice of the case requires it`

§§ `Motor accident (CTP) -- what damages, and what limits` -- situation: your CTP claim is being assessed

GIVEN `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER, `CPI for the September quarter 2001` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `CPI figures for the prescribed amounts`
`the September CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` `CPI for the September quarter 2001` MEANS
    `CPI figures for the prescribed amounts` WITH
        `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` IS `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident`
        `CPI for the September quarter 2001`                            IS `CPI for the September quarter 2001`

GIVEN `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July` IS A NUMBER, `CPI for the March quarter 2013` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `CPI figures for s 52(7)`
`the March CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July` `CPI for the March quarter 2013` MEANS
    `CPI figures for s 52(7)` WITH
        `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` IS `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July`
        `CPI for the March quarter 2013`                                       IS `CPI for the March quarter 2013`

@export What damages for non-economic loss (pain and suffering, loss of amenities, disfigurement) can I get after a motor accident (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) ss 3(1), 52(1), (3)-(8); Civil Liability Regulations 2013 (SA) reg 7)?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident (the amounts in force then apply)
      `days my normal life was significantly impaired` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days your ability to lead a normal life was significantly impaired by the injury
      `my medical expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc The medical expenses reasonably incurred for the injury, in dollars
      `my injury scale value` IS A NUMBER @desc The injury scale value (ISV), a whole number from 0 to 100, that the court assesses under the Civil Liability Regulations 2013 (Part 2 and Schedule 1)
      `the court finds my case exceptional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your ISV is 10 or less, whether the court is satisfied that your non-economic loss is exceptional compared with others with the same injury and that the threshold would be harsh and unjust (s 52(5))
      `the ISV the court uses instead` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the ISV the court bases its assessment on (s 52(6): rarely more than 25% above your ISV); otherwise any whole number
      `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the accident year (for the prescribed minimum)
      `CPI for the September quarter 2001` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter 2001
      `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July on or before the accident (for an accident from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026, the March quarter 2025; ignored before 1 July 2014)
      `CPI for the March quarter 2013` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the March quarter 2013 (ignored for an accident before 1 July 2014)
GIVETH A `Non-economic loss answer`
DECIDE `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` IS
    `s 52 -- damages for non-economic loss`
        (`Non-economic loss facts` WITH
            `the day of the injury`                                              IS `the day of the accident`
            `days the ability to lead a normal life was significantly impaired` IS `days my normal life was significantly impaired`
            `medical expenses reasonably incurred`                               IS `my medical expenses`
            `the injury scale value`                                             IS `my injury scale value`
            `the court is satisfied under s 52(5)`                               IS `the court finds my case exceptional`
            `the injury scale value the court bases a s 52(5) assessment on`     IS `the ISV the court uses instead`)
        (`the prescribed minimum (CLA s 3(1))` (`the September CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` `CPI for the September quarter 2001`))
        (`the March CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July` `CPI for the March quarter 2013`)

DECLARE `Mental harm answer` IS ONE OF
    `damages may be awarded for the mental harm, and for economic loss from it`
    `damages may be awarded for the mental harm, but not for economic loss from it (s 53(3))`
    `no damages for the mental harm (s 53(1), (2))`

@export Can I get damages for mental harm after a motor accident (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) s 53)?
GIVEN `I was physically injured in the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were physically injured in the accident
      `I was at the scene when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were present at the scene of the accident when it occurred
      `a close family member was killed, injured or endangered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a parent, spouse, domestic partner or child of a person killed, injured or endangered in the accident
      `it is a recognised psychiatric illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your mental harm is a recognised psychiatric illness (a medical question)
GIVETH A `Mental harm answer`
DECIDE `Can I get damages for mental harm` IS
    IF NOT (`damages may be awarded for the mental harm (s 53(1), (2))` `my harm`)
    THEN `no damages for the mental harm (s 53(1), (2))`
    ELSE IF `damages may be awarded for economic loss from the mental harm (s 53(1)-(3))` `my harm`
         THEN `damages may be awarded for the mental harm, and for economic loss from it`
         ELSE `damages may be awarded for the mental harm, but not for economic loss from it (s 53(3))`
    WHERE
        `my harm` MEANS
            `Mental harm facts` WITH
                `the person was physically injured in the accident`                    IS `I was physically injured in the accident`
                `the person was present at the scene of the accident when it occurred` IS `I was at the scene when it happened`
                `the person is a parent, spouse, domestic partner or child of a person killed, injured or endangered in the accident` IS `a close family member was killed, injured or endangered`
                `the harm consists of a recognised psychiatric illness`                IS `it is a recognised psychiatric illness`

@export What is the most I can get for loss of earning capacity after a motor accident, given the court's assessment (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) ss 3(1), 54(1), (2), 56A(2), (3), (5))?
GIVEN `my past loss as assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc Your past loss of earning capacity in dollars as the court assesses it (after any reduction for your own contributory negligence)
      `the loss in my first week off work` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of that past loss for the first week you were incapacitated for work (0 if you were not incapacitated)
      `my future loss as assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc Your future loss of earning capacity in dollars as the court assesses it (after the discount rate and contributory negligence)
      `my injury scale value` IS A NUMBER @desc The injury scale value (ISV) the court assesses (0 to 100)
      `the court finds my case exceptional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your ISV is 7 or less, whether the court is satisfied the consequences for your future earning capacity are exceptional and the threshold would be harsh and unjust (s 56A(3))
      `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the accident year (for the prescribed maximum)
      `CPI for the September quarter 2001` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter 2001
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can get for loss of earning capacity` IS
    `ss 54, 56A -- damages for loss of earning capacity`
        (`Earning capacity facts` WITH
            `past loss of earning capacity as assessed`       IS `my past loss as assessed`
            `the part of it for the first week of incapacity`  IS `the loss in my first week off work`
            `future loss of earning capacity as assessed`     IS `my future loss as assessed`
            `the injury scale value for earning capacity`     IS `my injury scale value`
            `the court is satisfied under s 56A(3)`            IS `the court finds my case exceptional`)
        (`the prescribed maximum (CLA s 3(1))` (`the September CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` `CPI for the September quarter 2001`))

@export What is the most I can get for lost superannuation contributions after a motor accident (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) s 56A(6)-(9))?
GIVEN `my damages for loss of earning capacity` IS A NUMBER @desc Your damages for the loss of the earning capacity on which the superannuation contributions are based, in dollars (see "What is the most I can get for loss of earning capacity")
      `the minimum superannuation percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The minimum percentage of earnings the law requires an employer to pay as superannuation contributions (the superannuation guarantee rate, as a fraction, for example 0.12 for 12%)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can get for lost superannuation` IS
    `s 56A(6), (8) -- the most for lost superannuation contributions` `my damages for loss of earning capacity` `the minimum superannuation percentage`

@export Can I get damages for the care my family gives me free of charge after a motor accident, and what is the most (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) s 58(1)-(4); Civil Liability Regulations 2013 (SA) regs 18, 19)?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident (the hourly rate in force then applies)
      `who cares for me` IS A `Who gives the gratuitous services` @desc Who gives you the free (gratuitous) services: a parent, your spouse, your domestic partner, a child, or someone else
      `my injury scale value` IS A NUMBER @desc The injury scale value (ISV) the court assesses (0 to 100)
      `hours of care a week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week the services are, or will be, given
      `months of care in a row` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many consecutive months the services are, or will be, given
      `weeks of care claimed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of services you claim for
      `the hourly rate claimed` IS A NUMBER @desc The hourly rate in dollars used to value the services
      `State average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The male full-time adult average weekly ordinary time earnings for South Australia published by the ABS, in dollars (reg 18)
      `the court finds paid care would be needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied the services are reasonably required and that, without them, someone would have to be paid to provide them (s 58(3))
      `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July on or before the accident (ignored before 1 July 2014)
      `CPI for the March quarter 2013` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the March quarter 2013 (ignored before 1 July 2014)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can get for my family's care` IS
    `s 58 -- the most damages for gratuitous services`
        (`Gratuitous services facts` WITH
            `who gives the services`                                IS `who cares for me`
            `the injury scale value for gratuitous services`        IS `my injury scale value`
            `hours of services a week`                              IS `hours of care a week`
            `consecutive months the services are or will be given`  IS `months of care in a row`
            `weeks of services claimed`                             IS `weeks of care claimed`
            `the hourly rate claimed`                               IS `the hourly rate claimed`
            `State average weekly earnings`                         IS `State average weekly earnings`
            `the court is satisfied under s 58(3)`                  IS `the court finds paid care would be needed`)
        (`the reg 19 hourly rate for an injury on` `the day of the accident` (`the March CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July` `CPI for the March quarter 2013`))

@export After a death in a motor accident, what is the most the dependants can get for loss of financial support, given the court's assessment (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) ss 54(3), 58B(3))?
GIVEN `the loss of financial support as assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc The dependants' loss of financial support in dollars as the court assesses it (after the discount rate and any contributory negligence)
      `earning capacity damages the deceased received` IS A NUMBER @desc Damages for loss of earning capacity the deceased received before death, in dollars (0 if none)
      `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the accident year (for the prescribed maximum)
      `CPI for the September quarter 2001` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter 2001
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the dependants can get` IS
    `ss 54(3), 58B -- damages for loss of financial support after a death` `the loss of financial support as assessed` `earning capacity damages the deceased received` (`the prescribed maximum (CLA s 3(1))` (`the September CPI figures I gave` `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` `CPI for the September quarter 2001`))
